    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d746">

                <pb facs="0807" n="795" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg795"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/27216</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5401</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-09">January 9, 1943</date>.<lb/>[Received January
                        16.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my despatch No. 5386 of
                    January 7, 1943,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d746-f1"/> with which I enclosed a
                    memorandum of my conversation with Dr. Raul Morales Beltramí,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d746-f2"/> in which he outlined to me the contemplated steps which
                    would proceed [<hi rendition="#italic">precede</hi>] the break of relations
                    between Chile and the Axis powers, I have the honor to report that to date the
                    plan explained by Dr. Morales has been followed: the President of the
                        Republic,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d746-f3"/> accompanied by his Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs, Dr. Joaquin Fernández Fernández, left last night for Viña del
                    Mar, and the papers announced for next week a Cabinet meeting and a meeting of
                    the Senate at which the Foreign Minister would explain the proposed change in
                    Chile’s international policy.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Minister sent word to me yesterday that everything was progressing
                    rapidly toward the break.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Claude G. Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
